Source: ajv4l2
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Max Lapshin <max@flussonic.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), dh-dkms
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/flussonic/aja-v4l2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: ajv4l2-dkms
Architecture: all
Depends: dkms, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: linux-headers-generic | linux-headers-amd64 | linux-headers-arm64
Description: V4L2 driver for AJA SDI cards (DKMS source)
 Every SDI input of an AJA card (KONA 5 and relatives) gets a multi-planar
 V4L2 capture node whose buffers carry the picture, the frame's audio, the
 ancillary data packets and per-frame metadata, by the SDI frame contract
 shared with our other SDI drivers.
 .
 The module is built by DKMS for every installed kernel. The package keeps
 ajantv2, the other driver of these cards, from autoloading, since
 whichever loads first owns them.

Package: ajv4l2-dev
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: V4L2 driver for AJA SDI cards (client headers)
 The headers a program needs to read the buffers of the ajv4l2 nodes:
 sdi_av.h, the frame contract (pixel formats, the layout of the audio and
 ancillary data planes and the per-frame metadata), and ajav.h, the
 card's own block of the metadata.
